{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>You shall not plow with an ox and a donkey</b> — clean and unclean. A hint that a righteous person should not partner with a wicked person." "<b>תחרוש</b> — two times, and the other: <b>do not plot evil against your fellow</b> (לא תחרוש על רעך רעה). This explains the reason for not plowing with an ox and a donkey: because the ox chews the cud and the donkey does not chew the cud, and when the ox is seen chewing the cud it will suppose that it is eating and suffer. And this is <b>do not plot evil against your fellow</b> — for it causes the donkey that plows to suffer evil against its fellow:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:17.497664595Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}